@@ -40,7 +40,25 @@ used.
 
 Returns events sorted by start time, each with `id, accountId,
 calendarId, subject, start_utc/start_local, end_utc/end_local,
-location, attendees, isAllDay, organizer`.
+location, attendees, isAllDay, organizer, showAs, isCancelled, responseStatus`.
+
+### Availability and "Show as"
+
+Both list and detail reads expose `showAs`: `free`, `tentative`, `busy`,
+`outOfOffice`, `workingElsewhere`, or `unknown` when the provider did not
+supply a usable value. Microsoft 365 and Outlook.com preserve Graph's
+availability; Google transparency, iCalendar TRANSP, and JSON showAs use
+the corresponding provider semantics.
+
+A `free` event does not block a meeting even when it is all-day. A cancelled
+event (`isCancelled=true`) does not block either. Presence on the calendar,
+its title, and all-day duration alone do not establish unavailability.
+Assess tentative events and working-elsewhere locations in context.
+
+For `unknown`, retrieve the exact occurrence's details or ask about a
+material unresolved conflict; never report an invented `busy` status or
+assume unknown means free. Use `responseStatus` to distinguish attendance
+responses from the separate availability and cancellation fields.
 
 ### `get_calendar_event_details(accountId, calendarId, eventId, timeZone)`
 
